tion":{"commit_sha":"6262772f9bacf0d209fa4aac0519728184fb96f0","position":"1788491726754834838-8e9f8ab4-4a68-45a8-913d-97b6af8010db"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ab2944801e3c8db635c7b87921c91d0b811c05c2acb2fe4012b934a07e01240b","event_uuid":"81f25bd1-07dc-4b7a-b520-24d696f66a25","position":{"commit_sha":"f2debe1356d4c114b3220dd43252d8ebc6e4b3b3","position":"1788496957306471409-81f25bd1-07dc-4b7a-b520-24d696f66a25"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"46c332742cbd81ee4017fb573c3296a11f61757bf852267e0789d1cfcc60035b","event_uuid":"85a7c4f3-fa6b-4722-879b-d67151373a66","position":{"commit_sha":"c1a645219c4e6b0112c3e83ba7969ecfd6d955a7","position":"1788497849725982255-85a7c4f3-fa6b-4722-879b-d67151373a66"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pinned upstream API evidence (2026-09-03)\n\nVerified directly against the python-hcl2 v8.1.3 tag:\n- `hcl2/api.py` imports `SerializationOptions` from `hcl2.utils`; `load`/`loads` accept `serialization_options` and pass it into serialization.\n- `hcl2/utils.py` defines the `SerializationOptions` dataclass, its `with_meta: bool = False` field, and the exact emitted metadata names `__start_line__` / `__end_line__`.\n- The pinned getting-started guide documents `SerializationOptions(with_meta=True)` with those exact keys.\n\nSources:\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/api.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/utils.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/docs/01_getting_started.md\n\nThe implementation tests still exercise the installed 8.1.3 package through the real parser boundary; this note establishes that the planned symbol, parameter, and key spellings are source-verified rather than recalled.","timestamp":1788475643015016781},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Correction to the preceding metadata note (2026-09-03)\n\nThe v8.1.3 source comment on `SerializationOptions.with_meta` is not matched by serialized behavior. An isolated import probe against the exact `python-hcl2==8.1.3` wheel parsed:\n\n`variable \"x\" {\\n  type = string\\n}`\n\nObserved:\n- `loads(..., serialization_options=SerializationOptions(with_meta=True))` returned block data with `__is_block__` but no `__start_line__`/`__end_line__`.\n- Public `parses_to_tree(...)` returned raw Lark nodes whose `Tree.meta` ranges were block `1:1–3:2` and attribute `2:2–2:15`.\n\nThe revised plan therefore uses `hcl2.parses_to_tree` plus public Lark `Tree.meta` and explicitly forbids reliance on serialized metadata. This note supersedes the prior claim that `with_meta=True` emits the line keys. Source: https://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/api.py","timestamp":1788476253576397643},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pinned API evidence addendum (2026-09-03)\n\nThe exact v8.1.3 public and positional preconditions are:\n- `hcl2.api.parses_to_tree(text: str) -> Tree` (distinct from `parse_to_tree(file: TextIO)`) and it is exported by `hcl2.__init__`.\n- `hcl2.parser.parser()` constructs Lark with `propagate_positions=True`.\n- An isolated exact-wheel invocation of `parses_to_tree` observed `Tree.meta` coordinates block `1:1–3:2`, attribute `2:2–2:15`.\n\nSources:\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/api.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/__init__.py\nhttps://github.com/amplify-education/python-hcl2/blob/v8.1.3/hcl2/parser.py","timestamp":1788477299627701759},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Exact-wheel import probe result (2026-09-03; exit 0)\n\nCommand prefix: `uv --no-config run --isolated --no-project --with python-hcl2==8.1.3 python -c <probe>`\n\nObserved stdout:\n```\n8.1.3\n(text: str) -> lark.tree.Tree\nTrue\n[('block', 1, 1, 3, 2), ('attribute', 2, 2, 2, 15)]\n['__is_block__']\n```\n\nThe lines are respectively distribution version; `inspect.signature(parses_to_tree)`; `parser().options.propagate_positions`; raw `Tree.meta` coordinates; and serialized metadata-like keys from `loads(..., SerializationOptions(with_meta=True))`.","timestamp":1788478312726649127}],"created_at":1788469424717431454,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8f9e52d5-0a96-487c-8263-ff8abd747c5a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"},{"link_uuid":"55e3fa84-fcdb-449b-a1e3-481cf9f6ed6b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8193-e0f3-9f88-4272"},{"link_uuid":"8e9f8ab4-4a68-45a8-913d-97b6af8010db","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"884d-01e1-4178-471e"},{"link_uuid":"85a7c4f3-fa6b-4722-879b-d67151373a66","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"536f-10e3-bde4-48d9"}],"description":"## Context\n\nPurpose: conservative module-wide Terraform evidence for T10 Pass 1 and independent Pass 2.\n\n## Scope\n\n### Optional boundary\n\nAdd `grounding-terraform = [\"python-hcl2==8.1.3\"]` and the `hcl2` probe. In `_capabilities.py`, add `grounding-terraform` to `DECLARED_EXTRAS` and register ABSTAIN-posture `grounding_terraform`. It is sole opt-in; core/non-Terraform paths import/advertise nothing. Extend optionality CI.\n\n### Structural index\n\nAdd `terraform_index.py`/`terraform_tools.py`. Each call owns cache+ledger; its finalizer frees them. Pass 2 re-captures the frozen source; no cache crosses steps.\n\n- Trigger on impacted `.tf`/`.tf.json`, or Terraform/OpenTofu plan plus repo Terraform. Index affected directories; follow repo-contained literal children/reverse callers; exclude VCS, virtualenv, `.terraform/`.\n- Directly inspect a changed `.tfvars`, but never infer it is selected.\n- Reject absolute/out-of-repo sources and escaping symlinks. Enforce 64 modules, 5,000 files, 32 MiB, and the existing 60-second deadline before returning facts; any failure yields one abstention with no partial facts.\n- Exact-wheel import probe exited 0: `8.1.3`; `parses_to_tree` signature `(text: str) -> lark.tree.Tree`; `parser().options.propagate_positions=True`; `Tree.meta` block `(1,1,3,2)`, attribute `(2,2,2,15)`; serialized meta keys `['__is_block__']`. Use `parses_to_tree` on strict-UTF-8-decoded bytes; JSON uses unambiguous key range, else file-level. Full command/output: ticket evidence comment dated 2026-09-03.\n\n### Operations and schemas\n\n- `lookup_declaration(address, module_path=\"\")`: variable, local, output, module, provider, managed resource, data resource.\n- `resolve_reference(reference, from_file)`: direct module traversals/repo-local child outputs; resource bases may resolve, provider attributes never do.\n- Both are `job=refute`: static resolution returns `refuted` at T1; all non-proof is `abstain`; neither emits `match` or asserts absence.\n- Grounding references use `kind=\"symbol\"` for declarations and `kind=\"member\"` for dotted traversals, with canonical address as `name` and `language=\"terraform\"`. Closed `terraform_kind`: `variable|local|output|module|provider|managed_resource|data_resource`.\n- Normalize paths to NFC repo-relative POSIX (empty module `.`; collapse dots; preserve case; reject NUL/absolute/escaping `..`). Trim outer address whitespace, grammar-parse, and case-preserving dot-render; internal whitespace, splats, or computed indexes abstain.\n\nAdd closed `terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json`; validate evidence against `grounding.schema.json` and receipts against it. Required receipt fields: `schema_version`, `operation`, normalized `query`, `snapshot_digest`, `module_digest`, `backend` (parser/version, analyzer/version, config digest), `limits`, `outcome`, generic `reason`, closed `reason_detail`, and `result_digest`. Snapshot/module SHA-256 uses a sorted length-prefixed path+byte stream. Config/result reuse `\"sha256:\" + rebar._store.canonical.content_hash(float_free_object)`. Refuted hashes safe facts; abstain hashes exactly `{outcome,reason,reason_detail}`.\n\nWorked receipt (digests abbreviated only here):\n\n`{\"schema_version\":1,\"operation\":\"lookup_declaration\",\"query\":{\"address\":\"module.web\",\"module\":\"infra\"},\"snapshot_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"module_digest\":\"sha256:…\",\"backend\":{\"parser\":\"python-hcl2\",\"parser_version\":\"8.1.3\",\"analyzer\":\"rebar-terraform-structural\",\"analyzer_version\":1,\"config_digest\":\"sha256:…\"},\"limits\":{\"modules\":64,\"files\":5000,\"bytes\":33554432,\"timeout_ms\":60000},\"outcome\":\"refuted\",\"reason\":null,\"reason_detail\":null,\"result_digest\":\"sha256:…\"}`\n\nWorked abstain (same required provenance): `{\"operation\":\"resolve_reference\",\"query\":{\"reference\":\"aws_instance.web.id\",\"from_file\":\"infra/main.tf\"},\"outcome\":\"abstain\",\"reason\":\"ambiguous\",\"reason_detail\":\"provider_attribute\",\"result_digest\":\"sha256:…\"}`.\n\nExact abstention translation:\n\n- Missing extra → `no_tool/missing_extra`; wrong parser version → `version_skew/parser_version`; non-Terraform call → `unsupported_lang/not_terraform`.\n- Pre-worker invalid/undecodable input → `parse_error/invalid_input`; unreadable capture → `parse_error/unreadable_file`.\n- Harness `timeout` → `timeout/worker_timeout`; harness `parse_error` (including indistinguishable native signal death) → `parse_error/invalid_input`; harness `other` from raise/no-result/protocol failure → `other/worker_failure`.\n- Duplicate address → `ambiguous/duplicate_address`; no unique hit → `ambiguous/no_unique_address`; dynamic source/expression → `ambiguous/dynamic_source|dynamic_expression`; computed value → `ambiguous/computed_value`; provider attribute → `ambiguous/provider_attribute`; splat/index → `ambiguous/splat_index`; unknown tfvars selection → `ambiguous/unknown_tfvars`.\n- Absolute/out-of-repo/escaping symlink → `private_or_internal_suspected/path_outside_snapshot`.\n- Module/file/byte bound → `other/module_limit|file_limit|byte_limit`.\n\nReturn only safe classes, hashes, and repo-relative locations—never credentials or literal payloads.\n\n### Plan-review integration\n\nInject tools only into Terraform T10 Pass 1. Terraform evidence selects Pass 2 with a fresh ledger and required independent query; inject no Pass-1 answer. Add a per-call tool provider/finalizer to `RunnerAgentStep`, preserving static `extra_tools`.\n\nRecord concrete reads as synthetic `read_file` usage and signed `**/*.tf`/`**/*.tf.json` membership, so sibling additions alter stdlib-only freshness. Missing extra exposes no tools; failures abstain.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nReuse existing seams; never scan or evaluate Terraform.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nRegistry/remote content, prompts, scanners, `terraform-config-inspect`, and Terraform/OpenTofu/provider execution.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Lean-install tests pin `python-hcl2==8.1.3`; absent-extra/non-Terraform routes import/advertise nothing.\n- [ ] Index tests find sibling files, bounded child/reverse callers, and keep targeted `.tfvars` unselected.\n- [ ] `lookup_declaration` tests assert exact `symbol`/`terraform_kind`, T1 `refuted`, line range, safe facts, and receipt.\n- [ ] `resolve_reference` tests assert exact `member` mapping and child-output resolution; computed/provider/dynamic controls abstain.\n- [ ] Boundary tests assert exact reasons/digests, no partial facts, cache/ledger retirement, worker reaping, and below/at/above bounds.\n- [ ] Workflow integration captures T10 Pass-1/Pass-2 requests with distinct ledgers; non-T10/non-Terraform controls expose no tool.\n- [ ] Signed-read-set tests observe all parsed files/patterns, then add a sibling `.tf` and observe freshness change.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py::test_no_forbidden_executables` observes no Terraform, OpenTofu, provider, tfparse, TFLint, Trivy, terraform-ls, terraform-docs, or other executable.\n- [ ] Schema tests validate evidence/receipts; `docs/grounding.md` and ADR 0111 document tools, trust boundary, outcomes/reasons, posture, limits, lifecycle, and prohibitions.\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Contract: REB-640, `docs/grounding.md`, ADR 0111, both schemas, harness `RunResult`.\n- Preconditions: sibling/child/reverse, dynamic, escape, bound, and harness fixtures.\n- Production: real capture/worker/response/request; fake only the model.\n- Tiers: parser/evidence unit-contract; workflow integration; lean-install subprocess.\n- Oracles: exact evidence/receipt/tools; no partial facts; cleanup; membership-digest change.\n- Controls: non-Terraform has no tools; literal resolves, computed abstains.\n- CI: `make test`, `make docs-check`, and optionality CI.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_capabilities.py && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make docs-check`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"pyproject.toml","reason":"declare the isolated grounding-terraform extra"},{"path":"uv.lock","reason":"lock python-hcl2 8.1.3 only for the optional extra"},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"exercise the new extra in isolation and union lanes"},{"path":"src/rebar/_optional.py","reason":"register the hcl2 import probe"},{"path":"src/rebar/_capabilities.py","reason":"register the ABSTAIN-posture semantic capability"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_index.py","reason":"bounded byte-snapshot Terraform structural index"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_parse.py","reason":"hcl2 parse-in-worker helper split from tools for module-size"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_receipt.py","reason":"closed receipt builder split from tools for module-size"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py","reason":"per-agent-call lookup/resolve tools, receipts, and usage finalizer"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py","reason":"merge synthetic concrete and membership reads deterministically"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py","reason":"T10 routing predicate plus Pass-1 hook and Pass-2 tool provider"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py","reason":"thread Terraform scope into T10 finder calls"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py","reason":"inject and finalize Terraform tools on T10 Pass 1 via RunRequest.extra_tools"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py","reason":"thread tf_provider through pass1_with_ladder to the production finder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py","reason":"thread tf_provider to run_pass1 on the live discarded-agent_runner path"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"route Terraform-evidence findings to agentic Pass 2"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/read_set.py","reason":"validate synthetic Terraform membership entries"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py","reason":"generic per-call extra-tool provider/finalizer seam"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"build the Pass-1 tool hook and supply Terraform-scoped tools to the plan-review verifier"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/__init__.py","reason":"register the TERRAFORM_GROUNDING_RECEIPT schema constant"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json","reason":"define and validate the canonical closed Terraform grounding receipt"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py","reason":"structural closure, limits, path, and parser oracles"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py","reason":"operation, receipt, redaction, and no-exec contract tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"Pass-1/Pass-2 routing and signed-read-set integration"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_terraform_pass1_production_wiring.py","reason":"held-out oracle proving tools reach the live gate via RunRequest.extra_tools"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py","reason":"lean import and dependency-closure regression"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_capabilities.py","reason":"extra/capability registry parity"},{"path":"docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md","reason":"record the accepted architecture and trust boundary"},{"path":"docs/adr/.numbers/0111","reason":"ADR number registry allocation for 0111"},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"regenerated ADR index including 0111"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document install, limits, routing, and evidence semantics"},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Install grounding-terraform extra in the REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS lane so the new hcl2 tests run instead of skip"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"Optionality suite item count 9->10 and hyphen-tolerant extras regex for grounding-terraform"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_change_input_not_an_outage_43d4.py","reason":"Test double accepts new tf_provider param on the extended run_pass1 contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py","reason":"Test doubles accept new tf_provider param on run_pass1/pass1_chunk"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pass1_finder_model.py","reason":"Test double accepts new tf_provider param on run_pass1"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"],["relates_to","536f-10e3-bde4-48d9"],["relates_to","59a7-cb88-f2f9-4148"],["relates_to","8193-e0f3-9f88-4272"],["relates_to","884d-01e1-4178-471e"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"d530ee6a-7b3b-4485-a7e3-933c23b35137","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["terraform","grounding","llm","optional","plan-review"],"ticket_id":"08ab-60d2-3082-4b47","ticket_type":"task","title":"Plan-review Terraform structural grounding vertical slice","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_capabilities.py","dd_id":"AC1","dd_text":"exact optional dependency, lean import, capability, and negative tool visibility"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_index.py tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py -k \"index or lookup or resolve or boundary or receipt\"","dd_id":"AC2-AC5","dd_text":"whole-module closure, line locations, schema mappings, closed reasons, bounds, lifecycle, and reaping"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","dd_id":"AC6-AC7","dd_text":"T10-only Pass-1/Pass-2 tool sessions and signed read-set membership invalidation"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py -k no_forbidden_executables","dd_id":"AC8","dd_text":"all executable launch sites remain unused"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_tools.py -k schema && grep -q '## Terraform structural grounding' docs/grounding.md && test -f docs/adr/0111-terraform-structural-grounding.md","dd_id":"AC9","dd_text":"evidence/receipt schemas and documented Terraform grounding contract (docs/grounding.md section + ADR 0111; no make docs-check target exists in this repo)"}]},"source_event_uuids":["adcc444c-3d54-43c8-b10d-4e789a9bf74a","d530ee6a-7b3b-4485-a7e3-933c23b35137","c982bf72-ab7c-4976-a634-38aa1c8ae5ff","8f9e52d5-0a96-487c-8263-ff8abd747c5a","fc117f50-e6a0-4b17-bc3d-ffba3805f376","9b91ecee-12e3-443f-8d5e-7c75ef8026ef","55e3fa84-fcdb-449b-a1e3-481cf9f6ed6b","4b306c6a-eda2-447d-8348-9b5f4af663a4","8e9f8ab4-4a68-45a8-913d-97b6af8010db","81f25bd1-07dc-4b7a-b520-24d696f66a25","85a7c4f3-fa6b-4722-879b-d67151373a66"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788500259279220639,"uuid":"c3c00de9-1d25-4f2e-a5ca-93431736febd"}